latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 0 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> would mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/4424bda987ed8322821518478e0789c3d7989f46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde318799549e8d589925c29fc0d5b7be5ac684b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2Y + Z = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d23a85adfbffb95303b87ed4e018c014afeef319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 5 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> would mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87cf306d374b8ff1d972a2f8c4b0e9919e044f4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities. Thus, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/3/6b3019aa161a29f20e67e2a7660f20d82c8d2573.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be734ffc008f6e6edd78c63aa7eca11d1afb0e41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 5 + 4 = 7 + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" /> possibilities.\n</p><p>We could have also concluded the number of possibilities for each case by listing all the possible solutions and then counting how many there were. We then see that in total, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/5/c955d707db949339476b531e0b9c9ac83c87d948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 11 + 11 + 11 = 11 \\times 4 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"305\" height=\"30\" /> possible values.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in previous solutions, we can use the same process to find that each value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities. This means that the total number of possibilities would be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Of the answer choices, the only one that is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/850e859ac64e4bd86198ef55cbcd7a894dd5d7ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 44}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Modular_Arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Modular_Arithmetic)\">Solution 3 (Modular Arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Modular Arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This problem needs a solution. If you have a solution for it, please help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit\">adding it</a></span>.</i>  \n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr